! `h4-cycloid-90.in` with `nosym`: the free half of the pair.
!
! **The name is wrong and the file keeps it: this texture is a HELIX, not a
! cycloid.** The propagation is along `z` (the four atoms are stacked along it)
! and every moment lies in the `xy` plane, so `m` is perpendicular to `q` at
! every site -- a proper screw. A cycloid is the other one: its moments lie in
! the plane that *contains* `q`, so each has a component along the propagation
! direction. The distinction is load-bearing here rather than pedantic, because
! `CLAUDE.md`'s trap list rests on it -- a chirality projected on `q` is
! identically zero for a cycloid and *maximal* for a helix, so a reader who took
! this file as the cycloid case would get the opposite of the null they wanted.
! The filename is referenced by tests, `PLAN.md` and `MAGNETISM-NEXT.md` and is
! left alone; what is corrected is the claim.
!
! The same four-hydrogen 90-degree helix, run with no symmetry at all, so the
! density is whatever the wedge sum gives and nothing is averaged. It is the
! control the symmetrised run is measured against: the group the magnetic filter
! leaves (4 operations out of 16) is either exactly the texture's own, in which
! case the two runs agree site by site, or it is too large, in which case this
! one keeps a texture the other has lost.
!
! **The discriminator is a pair, and the singular values alone are not it.** Two
! nonzero singular values of the (nat, 3) site-moment matrix mean the moments
! still span a plane, which is what a helix is -- but that ratio is scale free,
! so it reads as a perfect helix on a cell whose moments have gone to nothing.
! The same chain at 3 bohr spacing instead of 5 gives singular values
! [3.24e-4, 3.23e-4, 1.4e-23]: planar to 1e-5 and collapsed by a factor of 450
! from iteration 1. What has to be asserted is the pair -- sigma_2/sigma_1 for
! the shape, and sigma_1 against its own value at iteration 1 for whether there
! is anything left to have a shape. `SCFResult.site_moments` is that matrix and
! `history` carries it per iteration, so both halves are available.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 12.0, celldm(3) = 1.66666666666667,
    nat = 4, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.10
    noncolin = .true.
    nosym = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6
    nbnd = 24
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-8
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H 0.0 0.0 0.00
 H 0.0 0.0 0.25
 H 0.0 0.0 0.50
 H 0.0 0.0 0.75
K_POINTS {automatic}
 1 1 4 0 0 0
STARTING_MOMENTS
  0.6000000000  0.0000000000  0.0000000000
  0.0000000000  0.6000000000  0.0000000000
 -0.6000000000  0.0000000000  0.0000000000
  0.0000000000 -0.6000000000  0.0000000000
